() Tj T*
(REGISTRATION AND ENROLLMENT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All returning students must complete course registration through the online portal no) Tj T*
(later than March 15th for the fall term and October 15th for the spring term. Registration) Tj T*
(submitted after the deadline is subject to a $75 late registration fee and is not) Tj T*
(guaranteed a seat in high-demand courses.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(New and transfer students register during orientation week, which begins the second Monday) Tj T*
(of August for the fall term. Students who miss orientation must contact the Office of the) Tj T*
(Registrar directly to arrange registration before the first day of classes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A student may add a course within the first five business days of the term without) Tj T*
(instructor permission. Dropping a course after the tenth week of the term requires a) Tj T*
(signed withdrawal form and results in a "W" on the academic transcript rather than a) Tj T*
(letter grade.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ACADEMIC POLICIES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The minimum cumulative grade point average required to remain in good academic standing is) Tj T*
(2.0. A student whose GPA falls below 2.0 for two consecutive terms is placed on academic) Tj T*
(probation and must meet with an academic advisor before registering for the following) Tj T*
(term.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Appeals of a final grade must be submitted in writing to the department chair within) Tj T*
(thirty calendar days of the grade being posted. The appeals committee will review the) Tj T*
(appeal and issue a decision within two weeks. The committee's decision is final and may) Tj T*
(not be appealed further.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Academic honesty violations, including plagiarism and unauthorized collaboration, are) Tj T*
(adjudicated by the Office of Student Conduct. A first violation typically results in a) Tj T*
(failing grade on the assignment; a second violation may result in suspension for one) Tj T*
(academic term.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CAMPUS RESOURCES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Wellness Center, located on the second floor of the Student Union, offers free) Tj T*
(confidential counseling sessions to all enrolled students. Appointments can be scheduled) Tj T*
(online or by walking in during business hours, Monday through Friday, 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The main library is open 24 hours during final exam week, and until 11 p.m. on all other) Tj T*
ET
